\f0\fs28 \cf0 For annotation purposes:\
\
1. Assume the board with coords aa (top left, or S19) and ss (bottom right)\
2. Divide in regions (4 corners, 4 sides between corners, centre) e.g. corners lines a-f AND n-s as X and Y. Sides anything between corners, center= anything higher than that towards the midpoint of the board (jj) [TODO establish if there are more elegant methods to handle spatial tagging]\
3. Define groups as either A. deterministically through establishing whether the stones are connected or B. using the ownership map if the map establishes any continuous connected path of which all values are above 0.1\
3a. Define number of own groups as the number of groups of current move\'92s player colour\
3b. Define location of group as max(location(stone)) using locations at point 2 to map each stone participating in the group\
4. Define strength of groups as the average score of ownership values of stones participating in the group. \
5. Define connectivity of a loose group as the  average value of non-occupied intersections within the group bounds (i.e. no extending beyond n.e.s.w. of the group)\
6. Define group influence area as the count of own colour ownership values around a group (unbounded but contiguous)\
7. Define influence strength as the average of ownership values around a group\
8. Define building territory as changing an empty (<abs(0.1)) ownership intersection into own colour >abs(0.1) value\
9. Define solidify territory as increasing the ownership values of previously owned intersections\
9. Define reducing territory as reducing count of opponent\'92s owned intersections\
10. Define invasion as a move on an opponent owned intersection which once played reduces opponent\'92s territory\\influence and increases one\'92s own\
11. Define weakening territory as reducing the average value of opponent\'92s ownership values in one area\
12. Define leaving a weakness as a move which makes a previously owned intersection become opponent\'92s ownership\
13. Define size of potential territory as ownership values <0.7\
14. Define size of solid territory as ownership values >=0.7\
15. Define direct sacrifice as a move which makes the stone just played become marked as opponent\'92s territory in ownership map [todo define timeline on when concepts are visible: pre, at move, after move]\
16. Define indirect sacrifice a move which once played makes an own stone become marked as opponent\'92s territory \
17. Define urgency of areas as the sum of the probability mass of candidates by area\
18. Define cut as any w-b\\b-w stone configuration which separates two groups [might revisit this definition later]\
19. Define only move if the policy0 only has 1 value\
20. Define rough intent as, for each policy move assuming it converts to a 10 in ownership, what would the resulting effect be on the current board state \
21. Define tenuki if the move is played in a different area of the board to the last move AND there are candidates which are closer to the last move\
22. Define connection as a move which either deterministically connects stones into a contiguous group or a move which increases connectivity but not influence area of a group\
23. Define extension as any move played next to (horizontally or vertically) an existing own stone\
24. Define liberties of a connected group as number of liberties the group has \
25. Define Atari a move leaves an opponent group of 1+ stones with only one liberty\
26. Define reduce aji as a move with increases previous own ownership over an opponent\'92s group of stones\
27. Define attack any move which decreases an opponents group strength\
28. Define killing attack any move which makes an opponent group become >=0.5 own ownership \
